-Rules 100130–100138 read Traefik's access log, which records the client IP (`ClientHost`). The local decoder `simovilab-traefik` copies that IP into `srcip`, the field that active responses use to block a client.
+Rules 100130–100138 read Traefik's access log, which records the client IP (`ClientHost`). The local decoder `simovilab-traefik` copies that IP into `srcip`, the field that active responses use to block a client. Because it is a child of the `json` decoder, `local_decoder.xml` ends with `simovilab-json`, which decodes every other JSON event (Docker listener, container logs). Without it those events lose their fields and their rules never fire. Keep it last.
 
 ### Active response
 
diff --git a/scripts/wazuh-manager-conf-es.sh b/scripts/wazuh-manager-conf-es.sh
index df927b2..0043e7a 100644
--- a/scripts/wazuh-manager-conf-es.sh
+++ b/scripts/wazuh-manager-conf-es.sh
@@ -564,6 +564,16 @@ LOCAL_DECODER=$(cat <<'XML'
   <regex type="pcre2">"ClientHost":"([^"]+)"</regex>
   <order>srcip</order>
 </decoder>
+
+<!-- Todos los demás eventos JSON: escucha de Docker (reglas 87900-87959), registros de
+     contenedores (regla 100100 y sus hijas) y el resto. Cuando json tiene hijos, Wazuh solo
+     extrae los campos de un evento JSON por medio de un hijo que coincida: sin este decoder
+     esos eventos quedan con el nombre json pero sin campos, y ninguna regla salta. No tiene
+     prematch, así que tiene que ir de último: toma todo evento JSON que no sea de Traefik. -->
+<decoder name="simovilab-json">
+  <parent>json</parent>
+  <plugin_decoder>JSON_Decoder</plugin_decoder>
+</decoder>
 XML
 )
 printf '%s\n' "$LOCAL_DECODER" > /tmp/local_decoder.xml
diff --git a/scripts/wazuh-manager-conf.sh b/scripts/wazuh-manager-conf.sh
index 242fcb5..e3b8c71 100644
--- a/scripts/wazuh-manager-conf.sh
+++ b/scripts/wazuh-manager-conf.sh
@@ -564,6 +564,16 @@ LOCAL_DECODER=$(cat <<'XML'
   <regex type="pcre2">"ClientHost":"([^"]+)"</regex>
   <order>srcip</order>
 </decoder>
+
+<!-- Every other JSON event: Docker listener (rules 87900-87959), container logs
+     (rule 100100 and its children) and the rest. Once json has children, Wazuh decodes the
+     fields of a JSON event only through a child that matches: without this decoder those
+     events keep the name json but lose every field and no rule fires. It has no prematch,
+     so it must stay last: it takes every JSON event that is not from Traefik. -->
+<decoder name="simovilab-json">
+  <parent>json</parent>
+  <plugin_decoder>JSON_Decoder</plugin_decoder>
+</decoder>
 XML
 )
 printf '%s\n' "$LOCAL_DECODER" > /tmp/local_decoder.xml
